# Off a record that a store in sight fills under keys that are not written, a plain build is told nothing at a read by key: the read is typed anything, no check stands there, and what flows on is held at the
# next door. Link's flow still says what such a read may find. Under CheckProofsAtRunTime with CheckDictionaryReadProofs that is listed and asked at the read: the lane of the stored programs says both
# and keeps its eye on it. CheckProofsAtRunTime alone, which --aot-harden=proof-checks is and servers ship under, makes no such proof: there is nothing to check, and nothing is paid.
# f2 = sumOf
# RUN(PLAIN): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# PLAIN-LABEL: code f2:Body
# PLAIN: ElemGet
# PLAIN-NOT: source=Contents
# RUN(PROOFS): walk f2 mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# PROOFS-LABEL: code f2:Body
# PROOFS: ElemGet
# PROOFS-NOT: source=Contents
# RUN(ALONE): walk f2 mechanisms=all testing=CheckDictionaryReadProofs
# ALONE-LABEL: code f2:Body
# ALONE: ElemGet
# ALONE-NOT: source=Contents
# RUN(LISTED): walk f2 mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,CheckDictionaryReadProofs
# LISTED-LABEL: code f2:Body
# LISTED: ElemGet
# LISTED: CheckProof {{*}}source=Contents
# -- source: main.cjs
